    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **276 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp11Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change stores telephone numbers as digits-only and normalizes before the uniqueness check. Three edits:\n\n1. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 normalize the telephone to digits-only at the start of the method (`owner.setTelephone(normalizeTelephone(...))`), so the stored value and the JSON returned in the `telephone` field are digits-only.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.isSameOwner`** \u2014 switched the duplicate check to `normalizeTelephone(...)` (strips everything but digits) instead of the whitespace/case `normalize(...)`, so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` collide. Added the `normalizeTelephone` helper (`replaceAll(\"[^0-9]\", \"\")`, null-safe).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 relaxed the `telephone` request-DTO pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$` so formatted input passes request validation and reaches the service to be normalized. (The `Owner` entity's own `^[0-9]{10}$` constraint still holds, since normalization runs before persist.)",
